cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research proposal, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ScaleGap-TH: The Accuracy-Compute Frontier for Thai Audio Deepfake Detection under G.711 Telephone Coding"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "punyo_o"
repository-code: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
url: "https://github.com/punyopan/ysc"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
abstract: >-
  A focused research proposal measuring whether G.711 telephone coding degrades
  small-capacity Thai audio-deepfake detectors more than large-capacity ones,
  with a bandwidth-only control, paired difference-in-differences estimates, and
  an on-device deployment measurement.
keywords:
  - audio deepfake detection
  - Thai speech
  - accuracy-compute trade-off
  - efficient inference
  - on-device deployment
  - G.711
  - telephone speech
  - anti-spoofing
